# COMPLEX-REENTRY-001 independent review

Accepted as a confirmed capability gap, not completed complex-task support. Fixed commit 4ca1fdb2882ae31da2fd3ec49ac77e1710c69a3e, parent a4465a388b73ce144035d9139afb48f61519163a. No product change.

Root independently checked all 215 sealed members / 5,550,573 bytes against sizes, SHA256 and Git blobs, plus the index itself (216 additions, clean checkout, only this verification directory). All 131 product source files match product commit 0ad59befeee43c2fad752e3bad2ee69f87af3136 and the frozen PRODUCT_BYTES.zip. Product identity remains 82dbf9b3a68e0c21d085ac8289ca0e504da567b4cce7300ce697d602c2e4f0c6.

The actual public MCP task requests only Object_01/Object_03 solid_relation. Its non-error response is partial and the fact is unknown / null / unsupported_solid_geometry. Raw socket capture has the same selected object IDs and revision, world metres and 48/96 plus 8/12 vertex/face counts. Root stripped the existing HUMAN_EYE_BLENDER_MCP marker to parse this result; the first read-only parser attempt omitted that marker and failed JSON decoding. No new product call or evidence change occurred.

Independent reviewer tc1_geometry_review directly recomputed original local-to-world vertices against the actual capture: maximum difference 0.0; oriented face multisets match. It independently checked nonconvexity and 48 coordinate planes per axis, source-loading script, original request, frame/RPC counts, preparation correction and owner records. It did not run the author's audit or adopt its 52/52 as independent proof.

The confirmed denominator is one private NativeSession, one public observation, one host capture execute and one close RPC; the other eight planned observations are not run. No QA patch, extra readback, model answers or warm/changed-state benefit was measured. An actual bound geometric rejection is distinct from request/transport errors.

Fixed source explains the gap: connected concave shells fail the convex-shell path, and generally rotated nonorthogonal geometry is outside the world-axis orthogonal fallback. The specific internal first rejection branch is a static inference, not an instrumented runtime trace. This tiny assembly is not blocked by the broad size budgets. Surface distance alone cannot determine solid overlap or containment.

Preparation had one allowed adapter change accepting root's active_dispatched status while retaining token/owner/caps/source/expiry checks. A second preparation error attempted launch before PLAN existed and failed before Popen; retain both failures and the limited evidence for that second event. Actual runtime had no restart or retry. Original 600-second deadline remained unchanged. Outer, stdio and Native owner records have exit0/reaped; controller self has no independent owner-wait. Worker unknown remains alongside a separate closed response; no invented universal cleanup success.

Completed author turn 01a1bb5d-2ee1-7bf1-97d9-21e424779297 lasted 1,973,678 ms (32m53.678s), within 45 minutes. QA outer 2.3921593 seconds and other nested intervals are not additive. Author/model fees and CPU/heap remain unmeasured. Root and independent reviewers made no new product/Blender calls.

Next scope: one general read-only closed triangular-shell classification candidate, allowing connected concave solids and through-holes. Reuse existing exact predicates/BVH and surface distance; do not encode this ring or expand the write collision solver. Preserve the old 1e-9-tolerance solid_relation contract. A new explicit zero-tolerance read-only classification may use a separate fact with an unambiguous public contract. First establish complete original-task capability and analytic counterexamples; only then build the minimum continuous comparison adapter. No model-consumption experiment or unrelated module is justified before that result.
